{"availability":"available","full":"orgTestCodacy11KRepos110MB/repo-4822-GFM","name":"repo-4822-GFM","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2023-01-31T09:38:32Z","updated":"2023-02-01T04:10:42Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://colab.research.google.com/drive/1EaQ5h4u9Q_MmDSFTDmFG0ZOeSsFuRTsJ?usp=sharing","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T04:51:38.756Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T04:51:38.756Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T04:51:38.756Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T04:51:38.756Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This is the official repository of the paper Bridging Composite and Real: Towards End-to-end Deep Image Matting.","This repository contains the code, datasets, models, test results and a video demo for the paper Bridging Composite and Real: Towards End-to-end Deep Image Matting. We propose a novel Glance and Focus Matting network (GFM), which employs a shared encoder and two separate decoders to learn both tasks in a collaborative manner for end-to-end image matting. We also establish a novel Animal Matting dataset (AM-2k) to serve for end-to-end matting task. Furthermore, we investigate the domain gap issue between composition images and natural images systematically, propose a carefully designed…","We have released the train code, the test code, the datasets, and the pretrained models in this code-base page. We have also prepared a Google Colab demo and inference code for you to test on our pre-trained models on your own sample images. For the datasets AM-2k and BG-20k, please follow the sections AM-2k and BG-20k to access. Besides, we prepare a video demo (YouTube | bilibili) to illustrate the motivation, the network, the datasets, and the test results on an animal video"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/orgTestCodac